WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.629
A new Star Wars movie is always going to generate
a certain amount of hype, but the upcoming

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:09.100
final installment in the Skywalker Saga may
just be the most anticipated film in the franchise

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:09.600
yet.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.040
Here's everything you need to know about Star
Wars: The Rise of Skywalker.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.680
The first trailer for Episode IX revealed
that the film was titled The Rise of Skywalker,

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.960
but that was just one of several surprises
that the teaser had in store.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.400
The opening shots find Rey showing off her
new abilities in a stand-off with a TIE Fighter

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.650
on a desert planet that is likely Pasaana,
a new location revealed by the coverage of

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.220
a set visit by Vanity Fair.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:36.020
Finn and Poe also get in on the action, and
there's also a cheeky shot of the droid D-O,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.180
BB-8's new companion.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.960
But one of the biggest takeaways from the
first teaser comes as a stinger at the end.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.800
Despite having been thrown to his seemingly
certain death by Darth Vader in 1983's Return

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.280
of the Jedi, it seems that Emperor Palpatine
is somehow coming back.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:53.420
The Episode IX trailer ends with a shot of
the Death Star's wreckage and Palpatine's

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:57.410
unmistakable cackle, implying that The Rise
of Skywalker will see a new generation of

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.000
heroes facing off against the Dark Lord of
the Sith.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:05.960
Palpatine actor Ian McDiarmid also appeared
onstage at Star Wars Celebration 2019 immediately

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.780
after the big trailer reveal, essentially
confirming his involvement in the movie.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.880
"Roll it again."

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:18.390
Like The Force Awakens and The Last Jedi before
it, The Rise of Skywalker is hitting cineplexes

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.740
worldwide in December.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.430
The trilogy-capper was originally scheduled
to be released in May 2019, but a series of

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.940
destabilizing changes behind the scenes made
that target unattainable.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.540
Not long after Disney removed directors Phil
Lord and Chris Miller from Solo: A Star Wars

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:37.470
Story, and sidelined Gareth Edwards on Rogue
One in favor of rewrites and reshoots supervised

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.720
by Tony Gilroy, Colin Trevorrow was also fired
from The Rise of Skywalker.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.479
According to The Wall Street Journal, Lucasfilm
president Kathleen Kennedy considered bringing

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:50.970
The Last Jedi director Rian Johnson back for
Episode IX at one stage, but the powers that

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.460
be ultimately opted for the steady hand of
J.J. Abrams instead.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:59.840
The Rise of Skywalker will be released on
December 20, 2019 in the United States, though

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.340
many overseas fans will get to see the film
a little sooner.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.460
The U.K., Australia, Brazil, and Argentina
are all getting the movie on December 19,

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.000
while residents of Italy, France, Norway and
Sweden can see the movie a day earlier than

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:12.500
that.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.040
You probably won't be surprised to learn that
Daisy Ridley, John Boyega, and Oscar Isaac

00:02:17.049 --> 00:02:20.159
are returning, they're the heroes of the sequel
trilogy, after all.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.500
But they'll be joined by a whole host of faces
both familiar and new.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:27.439
For fans of the original trilogy, one of the
biggest moments in the Episode IX trailer

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.220
was seeing Lando Calrissian back in the cockpit
of the Millennium Falcon.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.189
The Hollywood Reporter revealed that Billy
Dee Williams was reprising the role in July

00:02:35.189 --> 00:02:39.770
2018, but details of Lando's part in The Rise
of Skywalker were kept under wraps in the

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:40.500
months that followed.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.659
Many now believe that Naomi Ackie, who is
playing a new character named Jannah, will

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.060
be revealed as Lando's daughter during the
film.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.040
The up-and-coming British actress was asked
about this at Star Wars Celebration 2019,

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.620
and her noncommittal answer only served to
fuel rumors that she's a member of the Calrissian

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.120
family.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.200
She told IGN:

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.419
"Lando is a very charming man, so he could
have children all over the universe, that's

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.240
all I'm saying."

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:03.680
"You look absolutely beautiful.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:08.020
You truly belong here with us among the clouds."

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.980
Dominic Monaghan of Lost and The Force Awakens'
Greg Grunberg also both have roles in The

00:03:12.981 --> 00:03:17.459
Rise of Skywalker, and they aren't the only
Abrams alumni appearing, Mission Impossible

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.980
III's Keri Russell is also playing a new masked
antagonist by the name of Zorri Bliss.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.580
One theory that's gained a lot of traction
following the release of The Rise of Skywalker's

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.359
first trailer posits that the title isn't
actually referring to any single character.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.579
A number of people now believe that the word
Skywalker will become a term used to describe

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:38.200
members of a brand new order, one that is
at peace with both sides of the Force.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.500
As Inverse puts it:

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.980
"These people, from Rey to Kylo Ren, to that
little stable boy with the broom at the end

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.060
of The Last Jedi, will not be Jedi or Sith.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.560
They will be Skywalkers."

00:03:47.769 --> 00:03:52.020
Comments made by The Rise of Skywalker director
J.J. Abrams seem to support this theory.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.740
At Celebration 2019, Abrams told fans:

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.680
"This movie is about the new generation.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:00.680
What they've inherited, the light and the
dark, and ask the question about facing the

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.400
greatest evil: are they ready?"

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:08.060
In May 2018, a Reddit poster with an impressive
track record when it comes to Star Wars spoilers

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.100
claimed to have seen what was described as
a very early storyboard for Episode IX.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:16.519
This alleged production art begins some five
years after the events of The Last Jedi, and

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.700
it seems that, in that time, Kylo Ren has
managed to hoodwink the entire galaxy.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:21.580
The user wrote:

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.980
"Kylo Ren's rule over the galaxy is seen by
most as benevolent.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:28.220
Many within the Resistance itself are questioning
why they should even be fighting."

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.440
This post came hot on the heels of John Boyega
teasing that Finn would have a new hairdo

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.520
in Episode IX.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.320
He told Yahoo:

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.810
"I can't wait to start shooting the next and
final leg of the franchise.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.520
The first step is growing out my hair, so
you can wait for the trailer to see why."

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:45.060
This all but confirmed that the story will
catch up with Finn and the surviving members

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.020
of the Resistance sometime in the future,
but will five years really have passed?

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.620
That's what those earlier spoilers claimed,
but according to an article in Empire, it's

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.980
not exactly the case.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.090
In its official 2019 preview, the magazine
stated:

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:01.720
"John Boyega has confirmed [Episode IX] takes
place one year after the events of The Last

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.220
Jedi."

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.860
So while a time jump may be in effect, it
also might not be that drastic.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.520
After purchasing the rights to Star Wars for
more than $4 billion in 2012, Disney decided

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.280
to clean house in a big way when it comes
to the series' canon.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.479
Prior to the release of The Force Awakens,
the company declared that all Expanded Universe

00:05:18.479 --> 00:05:22.870
materials, essentially, anything that wasn't
depicted in the franchise's movies or television

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.940
shows, were no longer considered to be official
Star Wars canon.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:30.460
The Mouse House then set about creating its
own line of short stories, comics, and books

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.409
to tie in with the new continuity, and one
such release in the new Expanded Universe

00:05:34.409 --> 00:05:38.720
might just include a huge clue about a major
development for an Episode IX character.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:43.360
In the 27th issue of the Poe Dameron comic
series, a conversation Poe has with Rey and

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:47.180
Finn seems to confirm that he's been unwittingly
channeling the Force all this time.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.560
Marvel's Poe Dameron comics overlap with J.J.
Abrams' The Force Awakens.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:56.139
#26 explained how Dameron survived that crash
on Jakku and filled in what he did between

00:05:56.139 --> 00:06:00.160
then and rescuing Rey and Finn from the First
Order, but it was the following issue that

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.550
really got readers talking.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.860
In that story, Dameron admits that he's been
able to tap into some kind of "energy" while

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.100
flying, prompting both Rey and Leia to suggest
he's been using the Force.

00:06:09.289 --> 00:06:14.420
The seeds of this reveal were actually planted
in the 2015 series Star Wars: Shattered Empire.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.410
This prelude to The Force Awakens explains
how Luke Skywalker gave remnants of a force

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:23.300
sensitive tree to Dameron's parents, who used
them to grow a new tree at home on Yavin 4.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:27.600
Dameron even mentions growing up around this
tree, further foreshadowing his connection

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.220
to the Force.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:33.259
During The Last Jedi, Yoda showed up as a
Force Ghost to help troubled former student

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:38.189
Luke Skywalker come to his senses and embrace
his failures, a standout moment in the saga's

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:39.500
divisive eighth episode.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:44.360
Yoda was rendered in CGI for the prequel trilogy,
but Johnson chose to go back to basics and

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.800
brought in Frank Oz to operate a slightly
updated Yoda puppet.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.980
Creature designer Neal Scanlan said:

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.560
"We just felt that it was absolutely right
and proper that we create the puppet in the

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:57.760
closest likeness to the original and to give
Frank exactly what he had the first time around."

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:02.060
Renowned puppeteer Oz, who provides Yoda's
distinctive voice as well as his movements,

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:06.300
could also soon be adding Episode IX to his
impressive résumé, if a new report is to

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:06.800
be believed.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.880
According to the New York Daily News, a source
with apparent knowledge of the production

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:14.420
has revealed that J.J. Abrams is going to
bring Force Ghost Yoda back.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.600
The insider said:

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:19.310
"The success of the scenes featuring Yoda
in The Last Jedi were huge.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:23.560
Yoda will again appear as a ghost as he acknowledges
Rey's success and growth as a Jedi."

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:29.020
Lucasfilm's original position on Carrie Fisher's
inclusion in future Star Wars movies was pretty

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:30.960
clear, she wouldn't be appearing in any.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:34.300
Before the release of The Last Jedi, Kathleen
Kennedy told ABC:

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.640
"Sadly, Carrie will not be in [Episode] IX."

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.600
The idea that they could digitally render
a version of Fisher like they did with Peter

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:45.319
Cushing's Tarkin in Rogue One was quickly
ruled out after execs met with Fisher's daughter,

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:45.820
Billie Lourd.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.920
All parties reportedly agreed that it would
be disrespectful.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:52.979
At the time, bringing Leia back with unused
footage from The Last Jedi was also said to

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.500
have been off the table, but things have shifted
since then.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:59.980
Disney have since confirmed that Fisher will
indeed be in Episode IX, with J.J. Abrams

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.760
apparently set to use footage shot for both
The Last Jedi and The Force Awakens.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:08.740
According to ABC's Clayton Sandell, who spoke
to Carrie Fisher's brother Todd on podcast

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:12.700
The Resistance Broadcast, the family are very
happy about what Abrams has planned.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.560
"Wait a minute, where'd she go?

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.060
Bring her back.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.440
Play back the entire message."

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:23.059
The idea of Darth Vader returning to the big
screen in Episode IX might seem ludicrous

00:08:23.059 --> 00:08:27.180
on the surface, but it seems Disney has been
subtly paving the way for the iconic Sith

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.440
Lord to play some part in the upcoming installment.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.220
After reading Marvel's Darth Vader comics,
which chronicle the villain's first years

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:37.599
working under the Emperor, ScreenRant noticed
one small detail that could be foreshadowing

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.220
a future appearance in the movies.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.940
The ins and outs of becoming a Force Ghost
have been up for discussion among Star Wars

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.960
fans ever since Luke Skywalker passed on in
controversial fashion at the end of The Last

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:47.460
Jedi.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:51.260
The assumption was that returning as a Force
Ghost was something only those in tune with

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.440
the light side of the Force could do, but
shouldn't the Sith have their own version

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:55.200
of this phenomenon?

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.940
Turns out they do, and it was explained in
the pages of the Vader comic.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:03.170
In the story in question, Vader is gifted
a mask that once belonged to another powerful

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.640
Sith called Darth Momin.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:08.899
Momin's "residue" was still attached to the
artifact when Palpatine gave it to his third

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:12.780
and final apprentice, who used it to help
erect his castle on Mustafar.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:17.120
The forgotten Sith was able to influence others,
and tell his story to Vader, via the mask.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.120
ScreenRant's prediction is that Vader will
similarly influence proceedings in Episode

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.520
IX, seeing as his grandson Kylo Ren is in
possession of Vader's half-melted mask.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:30.080
The backlash that Ed Sheeran received following
his Game of Thrones appearance ought to have

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.360
put him off cameos for life, but if rumors
circulating in the British press are to be

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:38.220
believed, the award-winning singer-songwriter
has gone on to film a scene for Episode IX,

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:38.720
too.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:43.060
Sheeran abandoned his Twitter account after
irate Game of Thrones fans told him exactly

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.740
what they thought about him popping up as
a Lannister soldier in the season 7 opener.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:50.839
Luckily for Sheeran, fans won't be able to
spot his mystery scene in the upcoming Star

00:09:50.839 --> 00:09:55.100
Wars installment, because his famous red hair
will be hidden by a stormtrooper's helmet.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:57.720
Dan Woolton, executive editor of The Sun,
confirmed:

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:01.540
"I can reveal the world's most successful
male singer has been seen suiting up for scenes

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:05.750
to appear in Episode IX, which has been filming
at Pinewood Studios since August."

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:09.860
Sheeran won't be the first famous Englishman
to don the iconic white uniform on the sly;

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:14.220
Daniel Craig snuck into The Force Awakens
as a Stormtrooper in a scene with Rey, and

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.730
Princes William and Harry were in The Last
Jedi, though their scene only made the home

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.220
version as an added extra.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:23.080
According to London's Evening Standard, the
royals were cut out of the final movie because

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.080
they were just too tall to be stormtroopers.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:29.780
With appearances in Doctor Who and Game of
Thrones under his belt, veteran character

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:34.900
actor Richard E. Grant already had some major
fan cred when he was cast in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.840
As it turns out, he's a big Star Wars fanboy
himself.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:42.820
On the podcast Happy Sad Confused, the actor
opened about the moment J.J. Abrams told him

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:47.480
he'd be part of the final chapter in the Skywalker
saga, and revealed how he was so excited that

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:49.220
he couldn't actually take anything in.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:52.970
For a time, the most popular theory was that
Grant would be taking on the role of Grand

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:57.720
Admiral Thrawn, a popular Expanded Universe
villain reintroduced into canon in the third

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.850
season of Star Wars Rebels, but the actor
outright debunked that rumor when the Radio

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:03.100
Times asked him about it.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:08.259
When Vanity Fair released a huge Episode IX
cover story in May 2019, the identity of Grant's

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:12.829
character was finally revealed, he's playing
a new villain named Allegiant General Pryde.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.260
As the magazine reported:

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:18.040
"The Oscar nominee promises to bring on-screen
menace and off-screen glee."

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:22.360
Most fans didn't love the fact that The Last
Jedi neglected to include the Knights of Ren,

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:26.400
a team of warriors first teased in the promotional
materials for The Force Awakens.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:31.120
Kylo Ren's band of fighters appear briefly
when Rey touches Luke Skywalker's lightsaber

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.730
and triggers a force vision, but they were
left out of Rian Johnson's follow-up because

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.620
he couldn't find a place for them in the movie.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:41.660
According to Vanity Fair's Lev Grossman, however,
The Rise of Skywalker is going to finally

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.920
provide some answers about the mysterious
gang.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:48.160
Fans got their first good look at these so-called
"elite fearsome enforcers of Kylo Ren's dark

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:52.670
will" in Annie Leibovitz's extensive photoshoot,
and what's immediately clear is that they're

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.020
not your typical Star Wars villains.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:58.560
In contrast to the sleek and shiny look adopted
by the First Order and the Galactic Empire

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:03.660
before it, the Knights of Ren wear dirty,
rag-tag armor and carry over-the-top weapons.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.340
Vanity Fair's Joanna Robinson wrote:

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:09.780
"Their D.I.Y. look, including one especially
lethal-looking gun arm, would be equally at

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:11.420
home in one of the Mad Max movies."

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.940
Their identities have not yet been revealed,
though fans think they have a pretty good

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.380
idea about where they came from.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.640
In The Last Jedi, Luke reveals that Kylo vanished
with a handful of his Padawan learners when

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:23.180
he set the temple ablaze and turned his back
on the Jedi.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.480
Did Luke's former students become the Knights
of Ren?

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:29.540
Now that the Emperor's involvement in The
Rise of Skywalker has been confirmed, it's

00:12:29.551 --> 00:12:32.449
safe to assume that he'll be involved in the
film's final battle.

00:12:32.449 --> 00:12:36.759
Who, where, and how he'll be battling isn't
really certain, but according to Making Star

00:12:36.759 --> 00:12:41.279
Wars editor Jason Ward, there's a huge rumor
doing the rounds that pits Kylo Ren against

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.140
Palpatine, in the form of Matt Smith.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.250
The British actor has been telling journalists
that he isn't in Episode IX, but that's a

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.820
claim that runs contrary to many reports about
the movie.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:53.720
Even international Disney websites are listing
the former Doctor Who star as being among

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:57.180
the cast, and Jason Ward believes that he'll
be playing a critical role.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.060
Ward reported:

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:01.760
"A really solid source over the years passed
on something they heard internally.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:07.060
The rumor is that Matt Smith isn't Palpatine
reborn or rejuvenated, but a dark side acolyte…During

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:11.420
the final act of the film, Rey and Kylo team
up to fight the Palpatine-possessed Matt Smith."

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:15.320
Ward's inside source claims that Kylo Ren
is possessed by the Emperor after killing

00:13:15.339 --> 00:13:18.270
his host body, leading to one last moment
of redemption.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:22.589
The tormented son of Han Solo and Leia Organa
has enough light left in him to lay down his

00:13:22.589 --> 00:13:26.620
arms so Rey can finish the job, becoming Ben
Solo again in his final moments.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:31.529
With Kylo Ren dead and Rey being apparently
too pure of a person for the Emperor to possess,

00:13:31.529 --> 00:13:33.540
the fight against Palpatine is won at last.

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:37.959
Luke Skywalker vanishes after helping Leia
and what's left of the Resistance escape at

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.780
the end of the The Last Jedi, passing on peacefully
into the Force.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:45.400
It was a highly divisive moment for fans,
and one that director Rian Johnson was forced

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:45.900
to defend.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:50.800
As the backlash grew, Johnson reminded everyone
that we may not have seen the last of Skywalker.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:51.800
He told Variety:

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.900
"I don't know where the next movie is going
to go.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:58.700
But it seemed like the potential of Luke crossing
into [a] new realm, that offers exciting possibilities

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.600
for the role he plays in the coming chapter."

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:04.800
Yoda returned as a Force Ghost in The Last
Jedi, and rumors that Skywalker will do the

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:07.660
same in the upcoming sequel have been around
for some time now.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:12.460
In 2018, Pinewood insiders claimed that sets
were being erected for two Episode IX scenes

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:13.600
involving Mark Hamill.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:14.940
An Express source claimed:

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.620
"This may well indicate that Luke will appear
as a Force Ghost to Kylo Ren and Rey separately."

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.680
Thanks to Hamill himself, this rumor can now
be classified as a spoiler, the actor has

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:27.029
since confirmed he's appearing as a Force
Ghost in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:14:27.029 --> 00:14:29.480
In June 2019, he told the Associated Press:

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.560
"The fact that I'm involved in any capacity
is only because of that peculiar aspect of

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:37.560
the Star Wars mythology in that, as a Jedi,
you're allowed to come back and make a curtain

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.110
call as a Force Ghost."

